lines 30/55/79/102) and `expect: pass` (lines 127/144/164/182), never `fire`/`no-fire`"],"finding":"The plan specifies `expect: fire` and `expect: no-fire` for the corpus cases, but those are not valid `expect` values: the eval loader rejects any `expect` outside ALLOWED_EXPECTS, and the fire/no-fire vocabulary is `finding`/`fail` (fire) and `pass` (no-fire).","group_criteria":["G1G2","G6","T8"],"group_id":"g8dc68416b1f11391","id":"f7f1cd06f9ed1f303","impact":1.0,"is_primary":true,"location":"`## The corpus` and Acceptance criteria lines 'exactly 4 cases with `expect: fire`' / 'exactly 4 cases with `expect: no-fire`'","norm_id":"nec024c2169243a5c","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A corpus written with `expect: fire` fails validate_dataset_and_gold / strict spec validation","The deterministic emits_valid_findings scorer and the recall/no-fire scorers key off FIRE_EXPECTS/NOFIRE_EXPECTS and will not classify a `fire` case as must-fire, breaking the gate"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Use `expect: finding` for NETMECH-F1..F4 and `expect: pass` for NETMECH-N1..N4, and reword the two ACs to 'exactly 4 cases with `expect: finding`' / 'exactly 4 cases with `expect: pass`'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Clarify whether the 'spec declares `criterion: project.net-mechanism`' AC targets the top-level `prompt:` key (which in this format would be `plan-review-project-net-mechanism`) or the per-case `criterion:` field, and align the AC wording with whichever the spec format actually uses.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[".rebar/evals/plan-review-project-portability.eval.yaml:11: `prompt: plan-review-project-portability` is the top-level criterion/prompt-naming key; `criterion: project.portability` appears only per dataset case (line 29)","src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:223 lists `criterion` among per-case `metadata_keys`, not as a validated top-level spec key","The plan itself lists `criterion` among the SIX per-case fields each case carries, implying it is a case field, not a top-level declaration"],"finding":"The AC 'The spec declares `criterion: project.net-mechanism`' names a top-level spec key `criterion`, but the top-level key that names the criterion/prompt in the modeled-on spec format is `prompt:`; `criterion` appears only as a per-case dataset field.","group_criteria":["G1G2","T8"],"group_id":"g157987239b2d3c3c","id":"f98e658f529abaee0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":true,"location":"Acceptance criteria: 'The spec declares `criterion: project.net-mechanism`.'","norm_id":"n5c0ef9bc66e7f4bb","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An offline test asserting a top-level `spec['criterion'] == 'project.net-mechanism'` would read a key the modeled-on format does not define at top level (it would be the `prompt` key, valued `plan-review-project-net-mechanism`)"],"severity":null,"