ct: finding` and `expect: pass` (lines 30,55,79,102,127,144,164,182); its test_calibration_metrics computes fires via `case.get('expect') in ('finding','fail')`","All four sibling project.* corpora (portability, failure-disposition-contract, engine-layer-enforcement, review-phase-boundaries) use finding/pass exclusively"],"finding":"The plan specifies the dataset label vocabulary as `expect: fire` / `expect: no-fire`, but the eval harness recognizes only `expect: finding` / `expect: pass`; with the plan's labels every fire case is scored as not-fire, so the corpus will not drive the calibration (and the operator-attested gate) it is built to prove.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":"g8dc68416b1f11391","id":"ffd795d1a4b79aa73","impact":1.0,"is_primary":false,"location":"Acceptance criteria ('exactly 4 cases with `expect: fire`' / '`expect: no-fire`') and '### Must-fire' / '### Must-not-fire' / 'The corpus' sections","norm_id":"nfcfb17f9529fbbba","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running `rebar criteria eval project.net-mechanism --runs 3`: all four F-cases carry `expect: fire`, fall through the `else \"pass\"` branch, and are expected to produce no finding — so a correctly-firing criterion would be scored as failing the fire cases (or the gate math yields n_fire=0)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace `expect: fire` with `expect: finding` and `expect: no-fire` with `expect: pass` in the two AC lines and the corpus prose, matching FIRE_EXPECTS / fixture_admission and the portability model.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Change the corpus `expect` vocabulary (and the two ACs) from `fire`/`no-fire` to the scorer-recognized tokens `finding` (must-fire) and `pass` (must-not-fire), matching `ALLOWED_EXPECTS` in src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_scorers.py:45.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan declares `expect: fire` and `expect: no-fire` (Must-fire/Must-not-fire bullets and two AC lines).","src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_scorers.py:32-33: `FIRE_EXPECTS = frozenset({\"finding\", \"fail\"})` / `NOFIRE_EXPECTS = frozenset({\"pass\"})`; `ALLOWED_EXPECTS` is their union (:45-47).","_recall (:221-226) returns _NA unless `expect` in FIRE_EXPECTS; _no_fire (:229-234) returns _NA unless `expect` in NOFIRE_EXPECTS — `fire`/`no-fire` match neither, so no case is scored.","The modeled-on referent uses the real tokens: .rebar/evals/plan-review-project-portability.eval.yaml:30 `expect: finding`, :127 `expect: pass`; its test keys on those exact values (tests/unit/test_project_portability_eval.py:107,116)."],"finding":"The corpus's `expect` value vocabulary (`fire` / `no-fire`) is not the vocabulary the deterministic `emits_valid_findings` scorer recognizes, so every case scores as non-applicable and the declared gate measures nothing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":"g8dc68416b1f11391","id":"f484ddb033edb7555","impact":1.0,"is_primary":false,"location":"Plan sections 'Must-fire' / 'Must-not-fire' and the ACs 'The dataset contains exactly 4 cases with `expect: fire`' / '`expect: no-fire`', plus the operator-attested eval AC.","norm_id":"n2c5556cb45a33149","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs `rebar criteria eval project.net-mechanism --runs 3`: every F/N case is _NA, the recall/no-fire denominators are empty, and the at_least(2) gate cannot be meaningfully met — the red proof proves nothing.","The offline test asserts '4 cases with expect: fire' against a spec whose values the scorer will never recognize, so the structural test can pass while the semantic gate is inert."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the dataset use `expect: finding` for NETMECH-F1..F4 and `expect: pass` for NETMECH-N1..N4, and reword the two ACs to 'exactly 4 cases with `expect: finding`' / 'exactly 4 cases with `expect: pass`', as the modeled-on portability corpus does.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabl